 "notes": "Wide-band 95% C.L. limit on kinetic mixing chi (red curve of Fig. 5), digitised from the vector figure results2_lin_final.pdf in the arXiv e-print (1053-segment red polyline, resampled to 100 points on a uniform mass grid with log-chi interpolation). Axis calibration verified two ways: curve endpoints match the quoted mass range 20.8-28.3 ueV (5-6.8 GHz via Eq. 3, f = 0.24 GHz x m/ueV), and the separate narrow-band red line sits at 26.38 ueV reaching chi = 4.26e-13, exactly matching Eq. 2 applied to the quoted narrow-band power limit 2.1e-21 W with the factor 2 for single-polarization detection. The narrow-band single-frequency spike (22.2 h at 6.331525 GHz, chi down to 4.3e-13) is NOT included in the points, which give the wide-band curve only. The excursion to chi ~ 9e-10 near 25.5-25.7 ueV reproduces the figure through the dismissed-data hole at 6.1-6.15 GHz. Assumes hidden photons are all of the local DM at rho = 0.3 GeV/cm3, unpolarized (random-orientation) HP scenario as in the paper.",
